  "summary": "The previous proposals converge on the correct diagnosis and fix locations, but the 500-char truncation is arbitrary and lossy — it will cut mid-JSON or mid-sentence, producing unreadable garbage rather than a useful summary. A better approach is to log a short structured message like 'Phase completed successfully' with the phase name and timestamp (which append_pipeline_log already captures), since the full output is already saved to conversation files and the pipeline_log's purpose is progress visibility in the web UI, not output replay. Additionally, the proposed fix misses error paths: when headless() throws or returns empty output (lines 306-316), no log entry is written, so the web UI would show a phase simply vanishing — an append_pipeline_log call with the failure message should be added in both error branches to give the user visibility into what went wrong."
